          %h3#translation_between_the_two_approaches Translation between the two approaches
          %p
            The
            %span.newWikiWord
              fundamental theorem on morphisms of schemes
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/fundamental+theorem+on+morphisms+of+schemes"} ?
            asserts that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
            from the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sch
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sch
            of schemes to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Aff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(Aff) \equiv Psh(CRing^{op})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            on the category of affine schemes, or equivalently on the opposite of the category of commutative rings, given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
