            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
            introduced by A. Rosenberg in terms of categories and covers defined using pairs of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nikolai+Durov"} Nikolai Durov
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stack"} Deligne-Mumford
            and Artin, the dg-schemes of Kapranov, the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
            = succeed "\u2013Vezzosi," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"} Toën
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+affine+spaces"} locally affine spaces
            in the fpqc, fppf or étale topology (Grothendieck),
            = succeed "," do
