            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiring+scheme"} semiring scheme
          %h3#underlying_topological_space_vs_underlying_locale Underlying topological space vs. underlying locale
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
            argues that underlying locale point of view is better than underlying topological space point of view, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes+as+locally+affine+structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} schemes as locally affine structured (∞,1)-toposes
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Terminology:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/EGA"} EGA
            says prescheme, for what we call scheme, and says scheme for what we call
